<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    intersection.tll.xml
    =====================
    Fully protected fixed-time signal program for junction "C", built
    directly against the linkIndex numbering and conflict, foes, matrix
    read out of the real generated intersection.net.xml, not assumed
    geometry.

    linkIndex map, confirmed from the actual connection elements in
    intersection.net.xml:
      0  = S-left  (S to W)     3 = E-left  (E to S)
      1  = S-straight (S to N)  4 = E-straight (E to W)
      2  = S-right (S to E)     5 = E-right (E to N)
      6  = N-left  (N to E)     9  = W-left  (W to N)
      7  = N-straight (N to S)  10 = W-straight (W to E)
      8  = N-right (N to W)     11 = W-right (W to S)

    Decoded foes, straight from the net.xml request block, all four left
    turns have an empty foe list and are compatible with every other
    movement at all times. The right turns have real, confirmed conflicts:
      S-right(2) foes  = E-straight(4), E-right(5), N-straight(7), W-right(11)
      N-right(8) foes  = S-straight(1), E-right(5), W-straight(10), W-right(11)
      E-right(5) foes  = S-right(2), N-straight(7), N-right(8), W-straight(10)
      W-right(11) foes = S-straight(1), S-right(2), E-straight(4), N-right(8)

    Note that S-right and N-right are NOT foes of each other, and E-right
    and W-right are NOT foes of each other, confirmed by their absence from
    one another's foe lists above, this is why they are grouped into shared
    protected phases below.

    This program is a direct, minimal correction of netconvert's own
    auto-generated 8-phase static program. The only change made is that
    the two right-turn connections in each main phase, previously given a
    lowercase g, permissive, yield-controlled, state concurrently with a
    movement confirmed to be their foe, are now held fully red during that
    phase and only receive green during their own dedicated protected
    phase. No other phase, connection, or duration relationship was
    altered beyond lengthening the two right-turn phases from 6s to 12s to
    compensate for losing their permissive supplement.

    Cycle length: 30+3+12+3+30+3+12+3 = 96 seconds.

    LEFT-TURN POLICY (changed 2026-09-13, deliberately)
    ----------------------------------------------------
    All four left turns previously ran in BOTH main phases, which the
    network's own conflict matrix permits: every left turn really does
    have an empty foe list and yields to nothing (verified by decoding
    the <request> block, not by trusting this comment).

    That permission rests entirely on PERFECT LANE DISCIPLINE. Each of
    the twelve movements is channelized into its own dedicated outbound
    lane - N-left lands in C_out_E lane 0 while W-straight lands in
    C_out_E lane 1 - so on paper they never touch. Real traffic of the
    kind this project models does not hold lane that precisely, and a
    left-turner crossing in front of a moving through-stream on the
    strength of a lane marking is exactly the conflict that assumption
    hides.

    So each left turn is now protected, running only in its own
    approach's phase. This costs left-turn capacity (roughly 60s of
    green per 96s cycle down to 30s) and is a deliberate trade of
    throughput for a safety margin that does not depend on discipline.

    Anything downstream that encoded the old shared-left structure was
    updated with it: decision_engine._PHASE_EXCLUSIVE_LANES, the
    left-turn scoring bonus, and emergency phase selection.

    NOTE: this file is a netconvert SOURCE and is NOT loaded at run
    time - intersection.sumocfg loads the compiled
    intersection.net.xml, which carries its own copy of this
    program. Both were changed together; change both or neither.
-->
<additional>
    <tlLogic id="C" type="static" programID="0" offset="0">

        <!-- Phase 1: North plus South, straight and left, protected.
             Green set: S-left, S-straight, N-left, N-straight.
             CHANGED 2026-09-13, see the LEFT-TURN POLICY note at the top
             of this file: E-left and W-left used to run here too and no
             longer do. -->
        <phase duration="30" state="GGrrrrGGrrrr"/>
        <!-- Phase 1 yellow clearance -->
        <phase duration="3"  state="yyrrrryyrrrr"/>

        <!-- Phase 3: North and South right turns only, fully protected.
             Green set: S-right, N-right. Verified conflict-free above,
             neither appears in the other's foe list. -->
        <phase duration="12" state="rrGrrrrrGrrr"/>
        <!-- Phase 3 yellow clearance -->
        <phase duration="3"  state="rryrrrrryrrr"/>

        <!-- Phase 5: East plus West, straight and left, protected.
             Green set: E-left, E-straight, W-left, W-straight.
             CHANGED 2026-09-13 as Phase 1 above, mirrored: S-left and
             N-left used to run here too and no longer do. -->
        <phase duration="30" state="rrrGGrrrrGGr"/>
        <!-- Phase 5 yellow clearance -->
        <phase duration="3"  state="rrryyrrrryyr"/>

        <!-- Phase 7: East and West right turns only, fully protected.
             Green set: E-right, W-right. Verified conflict-free above,
             neither appears in the other's foe list. -->
        <phase duration="12" state="rrrrrGrrrrrG"/>
        <!-- Phase 7 yellow clearance -->
        <phase duration="3"  state="rrrrryrrrrry"/>

    </tlLogic>
</additional>